; kat-token-handle.fk — a KAT-Coder-V2.5 token with the WHOLE 40-block forward in a Form cell.
;
; WHAT THIS IS. Block 0's front half went through the handle door yesterday (kat-block0-handle.fk,
; band 511). This cell is the rest of the model: the delta rule's back half, the gated norm, the
; 256-expert MoE, the ten full-attention blocks with their fused query-gate and partial RoPE, the
; exit head, and the greedy loop — every dispatch order and every binding decided HERE, in the
; body. No swiftc, no metallib, no host arithmetic on activations; the host crossings are
; metal_buf_from_file reading the model file's bytes and, once per MoE block, EIGHT ROUTING IDS
; coming back so the expert weight offsets can be bound — the decode-only bargain moe-msl.fk
; names ("nb02 * e is a number the host already has, because it is the host that binds").
;
; EVERY SEMANTIC BELOW WAS READ, NOT GUESSED — from the two references this file answers to,
; 2026-08-04: llama.cpp src/models/qwen35moe.cpp + delta-net-base.cpp (the arithmetic that
; CONSUMES this exact GGUF) and transformers modeling_qwen3_5.py (the parent the config names).
; The readings that would have been built wrong from this repo's own cells:
;
;   * THE CONV OUTPUT IS SILU'D before the q/k/v split (conv_output_silu = ggml_silu(conv_out)).
;     gated-deltanet-layer.fk does not carry this; the reference does, on both arms.
;   * VALUE HEAD h BORROWS KEY HEAD (h mod 16) IN THIS FILE. The HF reference repeat_interleaves
;     (h div 2), but the GGUF CONVERTER REORDERS the V-side heads (v, z, alpha, beta, ssm_a,
;     dt_bias, the conv's V channels, ssm_out's columns) from grouped to TILED order so ggml's
;     modulo broadcast is the correct mapping (_LinearAttentionVReorderBase, conversion/qwen.py:
;     "We reorder V heads to tiled order"). In this file's coordinates the mod is right and the
;     div is wrong — the exact opposite of the HF text.
;   * ssm_a HOLDS -exp(A_log) ALREADY (converter: `data_torch = -torch.exp(data_torch)`), so the
;     log-decay is g = ssm_a[h] * softplus(a[h] + dt_bias[h]) with NO negation here. Probed on
;     this file: blk.0.ssm_a[0..3] all negative.
;   * THE GATED NORM IS "NORM BEFORE GATE" (Qwen3_5RMSNormGated's own comment): per value head,
;     RMS over its 128 dims, times ssm_norm's weight, THEN times silu(z). The cousin order
;     (gate before norm, Mamba2's) is a smooth substitution no magnitude check would catch.
;   * THE DELTA READ SCALES q BY 1/sqrt(dk) (delta-net-base.cpp: `scale = 1/sqrtf(S_k)`), which
;     kimi-kda.fk's band-proven step does not carry because its caller owns the scale.
;   * FULL-ATTENTION q AND ITS OUTPUT GATE ARE INTERLEAVED PER HEAD: attn_q's 8192 rows are
;     16 x [query(256) | gate(256)], read at per-head stride 512 (ggml_view_3d with
;     nb1 = 2*head_dim). The gate is applied SIGMOID (ggml_sigmoid), after attention, before
;     attn_output — sigmoid HERE and silu on the deltanet norm is the split the 07-28 receipt's
;     cousin-trap warned about, and both nonlinearities are the reference's own.
;   * PARTIAL ROPE IS NEOX-SHAPED: pairs (k, k+nrot/2) within the FIRST nrot=64 dims of each
;     256-dim head, theta_k = pos * base^(-2k/nrot), base = rope.freq_base = 1e7. The KV's
;     dimension_sections [11,11,10,0] are M-RoPE sections; for TEXT tokens every section's
;     position stream is the same integer, so the section structure collapses to plain NEOX
;     partial rope — stated as this cell's radius: text decode only.
;   * NORM GAINS ARRIVE +1-BAKED (converter adds 1 to every norm.weight except the gated
;     ssm_norm), so every RMSNorm here multiplies the file's gains as they are.
;   * MoE: softmax over 256 router logits, top-8, renormalized over the chosen
;     (build_moe_ffn(..., LLM_FFN_SILU, /*norm_w=*/true, SOFTMAX)); experts are PLAIN SwiGLU —
;     the ldm form_swiglu_f32 the llama lane proved, which closes the pipeline map's gap 3 by
;     reuse; the shared expert runs beside them gated by sigmoid(ffn_gate_inp_shexp . x).
;   * BLOCK 40 IS THE MTP HEAD AND IS NOT RUN (nextn_predict_layers=1; the main pass is
;     blocks 0..39), full_attention_interval=4: blocks 3,7,...,39 are full attention, the other
;     thirty are linear.
;
; ONE SYNC PER MoE BLOCK PLUS ONE PER TOKEN. Each block's dispatches accumulate without waiting;
; the routing-id read is the block's single drain, and the argmax id read is the token's.
; Every mode-0 dispatch caps its threadgroup at 256 (the proven lane's measured number — the
; 2.9x that was hiding in tpg=0, receipts/2026-08-04-block0-door-and-the-256.md). The encoder
; is SERIAL: each dispatch's writes are visible to the next, so activations never leave the
; device between stages.
;
; STATE IS PER STREAM. Conv windows (one per linear block), delta states (32 x 128 x 128 per
; linear block) and the K/V caches (one pair per full block) are allocated fresh by
; kth-stream-state — metal_buf_alloc zero-fills (fk-metal-carrier.m memsets), so a new stream
; starts from the zero state without a zeroing pass.
;
; RADIUS, STATED: greedy only; text positions (no multimodal sections); maxpos bounds the
; stream; mla_round-family trig in the emitted rope is exact for the small positions a short
; prompt reaches (mla-msl.fk's own named radius). The end-to-end token has NO recorded oracle —
; the band gates every stage against fp64 references and the exit path against the recorded
; argmax-3637 mechanism witness, and claims exactly that.
;
; Kin: native/metal/kat-block0-handle.fk (the proven front half this extends),
;      native/metal/kat-exit-handle.fk (the exit path and its recorded 3637),
;      native/metal/llama-token-handle.fk (the loop shape, the 256, the copy kernel),
;      form-stdlib/gated-deltanet-msl.fk (conv/l2norm — the conv repaired today),
;      form-stdlib/moe-route-wide-msl.fk (the 256-wide router), form-stdlib/moe-msl.fk (the
;      gather bargain), form-stdlib/kat-coder-pipeline-map.fk (the ladder this climbs).
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk form-stdlib/str-byte-at.fk form-stdlib/equireach.fk form-stdlib/format-arith.fk form-stdlib/f16-decode.fk form-stdlib/q6k-dequant.fk form-stdlib/q6k-msl.fk form-stdlib/q8-0-msl.fk form-stdlib/q3k-msl.fk form-stdlib/q4k-dequant.fk form-stdlib/q4k-msl.fk form-stdlib/gated-deltanet-msl.fk form-stdlib/transformer-numerics.fk form-stdlib/trig.fk form-stdlib/tensor-ir.fk form-stdlib/jit-tensor-emit.fk form-stdlib/llama-decode-msl.fk form-stdlib/mla-msl.fk form-stdlib/moe-route-wide-msl.fk form-stdlib/equireach-gguf.fk form-stdlib/gguf-meta.fk form-stdlib/gguf-tensor-index.fk form-stdlib/kat-coder-embed.fk form-stdlib/metal-door.fk
;
; Proven by: form/native/metal/tests/kat-token-handle-band.fk

(do
    ; ================= the locally-authored kernels =================
    ; Each one either moves bytes, or transcribes arithmetic whose Form recipe is named beside it.
    ; The spine (fexp/fln/fsin/fcos/fpow, round) is ldm-msl-unit's — one definition in the unit.

    ; Q3_K dequant of ONE row out of the whole resident embed tensor. rowblk is the row's first
    ; superblock; the whole 540 MB tensor is bound once and a token is an offset, not a view.
    (defn kth-q3krow-msl (fname)
        (str_concat "kernel void "
        (str_concat fname
            " (device const uchar* qb [[buffer(0)]], device float* y [[buffer(1)]], constant uint& rowblk [[buffer(2)]], constant uint& n [[buffer(3)]], uint i [[thread_position_in_grid]]) { if (i >= n) return; uint b = rowblk + i / 256u; y[i] = q3k_at(qb + b * 110u, i % 256u); }")))

    ; q4m-matvec-body's exact fold with ONE addition: ebase, a flat weight-index base, so one
    ; bound 3D expert tensor serves all 256 experts and the gather is arithmetic on an offset
    ; (moe-msl.fk's own finding), not 24 views per token per layer.
    (defn kth-q4moff-msl (fname)
        (str_concat "kernel void "
        (str_concat fname
            " (device const uchar* qb [[buffer(0)]], device const float* x [[buffer(1)]], device float* y [[buffer(2)]], constant uint& rows [[buffer(3)]], constant uint& cols [[buffer(4)]], constant uint& ebase [[buffer(5)]], uint i [[thread_position_in_grid]]) { if (i >= rows) return; float acc = 0.0f; uint j = cols; while (j > 0) { j -= 1; float p = q4k_w(qb, ebase + uint(i) * cols + j) * float(x[j]); acc = p + acc; } y[i] = acc; }")))

    ; THE SAME OFFSET MATVEC FOR Q3_K — because the census SAID SO, not because the map did:
    ; probed 2026-08-04, blocks 5..35 quantize their routed experts Q3_K (type 11) while blocks
    ; 0..4 and 36..39 are Q4_K. The pipeline map's "ffn_*_exps Q4_K" was one block class's truth
    ; sampled into a claim about all forty; the first symptom was block 5's MoE answering 1e24
    ; (Q3_K bytes folded through the Q4_K decode — huge, finite, and green to every presence
    ; gate). The body had a Q3_K dequant (q3k-msl.fk) and NO Q3_K matvec anywhere; this is it,
    ; the family fold (j descending, p + acc) over q3k_at's superblock decode.
    (defn kth-q3moff-msl (fname)
        (str_concat "kernel void "
        (str_concat fname
            " (device const uchar* qb [[buffer(0)]], device const float* x [[buffer(1)]], device float* y [[buffer(2)]], constant uint& rows [[buffer(3)]], constant uint& cols [[buffer(4)]], constant uint& ebase [[buffer(5)]], uint i [[thread_position_in_grid]]) { if (i >= rows) return; float acc = 0.0f; uint j = cols; while (j > 0) { j -= 1; uint idx = ebase + uint(i) * cols + j; float p = q3k_at(qb + (idx / 256u) * 110u, idx % 256u) * float(x[j]); acc = p + acc; } y[i] = acc; }")))

    ; silu in place — the conv activation the references apply before the split (ldm-silu's
    ; arithmetic: x * 1/(1+exp(-x)) over the body's fexp).
    (defn kth-silu-msl (fname)
        (str_concat "kernel void "
        (str_concat fname
            " (device float* x [[buffer(0)]], constant uint& n [[buffer(1)]], uint i [[thread_position_in_grid]]) { if (i >= n) return; float v = x[i]; float sig = 1.0f / (1.0f + fexp(-1.0f * v)); x[i] = v * sig; }")))

    ; the deltanet gates, one thread per value head. A[h] is the FILE's ssm_a = -exp(A_log);
    ; softplus in the stable form gdg-softplus keeps: max(x,0) + ln(1 + exp(-|x|)).
    (defn kth-gates-msl (fname)
        (str_concat "kernel void "
        (str_concat fname
            " (device const float* a [[buffer(0)]], device const float* b [[buffer(1)]], device const float* A [[buffer(2)]], device const float* dtb [[buffer(3)]], device float* alpha [[buffer(4)]], device float* beta [[buffer(5)]], constant uint& nh [[buffer(6)]], uint h [[thread_position_in_grid]]) { if (h >= nh) return; float x = a[h] + dtb[h]; float ax = (x < 0.0f) ? -x : x; float sp = ((x > 0.0f) ? x : 0.0f) + fln(1.0f + fexp(-1.0f * ax)); float g = A[h] * sp; alpha[h] = fexp(g); float bb = b[h]; beta[h] = 1.0f / (1.0f + fexp(-1.0f * bb)); }")))

    ; the delta rule over ALL value heads in one dispatch, one thread per state row — the same
    ; per-row arithmetic gdm-delta-msl proved (decay, correct, write back, read the NEW state),
    ; with the head plumbing this model needs: alpha/beta from device buffers (they were computed
    ; on the device and may not cross), key head = h MOD nk (the file's tiled order), and q
    ; scaled by qscale = 1/sqrt(dk) at the read (delta-net-base.cpp).
    (defn kth-delta-msl (fname)
        (str_concat "kernel void "
        (str_concat fname
            " (device float* S [[buffer(0)]], device const float* c [[buffer(1)]], device const float* alpha [[buffer(2)]], device const float* beta [[buffer(3)]], device float* o [[buffer(4)]], constant uint& nv [[buffer(5)]], constant uint& dv [[buffer(6)]], constant uint& dk [[buffer(7)]], constant uint& nk [[buffer(8)]], constant float& qscale [[buffer(9)]], uint gid [[thread_position_in_grid]]) { if (gid >= nv * dv) return; uint h = gid / dv; uint i = gid - h * dv; uint kh = h - (h / nk) * nk; device const float* q = c + kh * dk; device const float* k = c + nk * dk + kh * dk; float v = c[2u * nk * dk + h * dv + i]; uint r = (h * dv + i) * dk; float al = alpha[h]; float pred = 0.0f; for (uint j = 0u; j < dk; ++j) { float sp = al * S[r + j]; S[r + j] = sp; pred = pred + sp * k[j]; } float err = v - pred; float bw = beta[h] * err; float acc = 0.0f; for (uint j = 0u; j < dk; ++j) { float sn = S[r + j] + bw * k[j]; S[r + j] = sn; acc = acc + sn * (qscale * q[j]); } o[h * dv + i] = acc; }")))

    ; the gated norm, one thread per value head: RMS over the head's dv dims (ascending
    ; sum-of-squares, Newton-50 from sdv — ldm-rmsnorm's own recipe), times the SHARED ssm_norm
    ; gains, then times silu(z). Norm before gate — Qwen3_5RMSNormGated's own comment.
    (defn kth-gnorm-msl (fname)
        (str_concat "kernel void "
        (str_concat fname
            " (device const float* o [[buffer(0)]], device const float* w [[buffer(1)]], device const float* z [[buffer(2)]], device float* out [[buffer(3)]], constant uint& nv [[buffer(4)]], constant uint& dv [[buffer(5)]], constant float& eps [[buffer(6)]], uint h [[thread_position_in_grid]]) { if (h >= nv) return; uint b = h * dv; float ss = 0.0f; for (uint j = 0u; j < dv; ++j) { float v = o[b + j]; ss = ss + v * v; } float meansq = ss / float(dv); float sdv = meansq + eps; float gg = sdv; uint it = 50u; while (it > 0u) { it -= 1u; gg = 0.5f * (gg + sdv / gg); } float inv = 1.0f / gg; for (uint j = 0u; j < dv; ++j) { float nm = (o[b + j] * inv) * w[j]; float zz = z[b + j]; float sg = 1.0f / (1.0f + fexp(-1.0f * zz)); out[b + j] = nm * (zz * sg); }}")))

    ; per-head WEIGHTED RMSNorm (the full blocks' q/k norms): same recipe, gains shared per head.
    (defn kth-headrmsw-msl (fname)
        (str_concat "kernel void "
        (str_concat fname
            " (device const float* x [[buffer(0)]], device const float* w [[buffer(1)]], device float* out [[buffer(2)]], constant uint& nh [[buffer(3)]], constant uint& hd [[buffer(4)]], constant float& eps [[buffer(5)]], uint h [[thread_position_in_grid]]) { if (h >= nh) return; uint b = h * hd; float ss = 0.0f; for (uint j = 0u; j < hd; ++j) { float v = x[b + j]; ss = ss + v * v; } float meansq = ss / float(hd); float sdv = meansq + eps; float gg = sdv; uint it = 50u; while (it > 0u) { it -= 1u; gg = 0.5f * (gg + sdv / gg); } float inv = 1.0f / gg; for (uint j = 0u; j < hd; ++j) { out[b + j] = (x[b + j] * inv) * w[j]; }}")))

    ; deinterleave the fused query||gate projection: per-head stride 2*hd, slice at off.
    ; A move, no arithmetic (llama's copy precedent).
    (defn kth-qsplit-msl (fname)
        (str_concat "kernel void "
        (str_concat fname
            " (device const float* s [[buffer(0)]], device float* d [[buffer(1)]], constant uint& n [[buffer(2)]], constant uint& hd [[buffer(3)]], constant uint& off [[buffer(4)]], uint i [[thread_position_in_grid]]) { if (i >= n) return; uint h = i / hd; uint j = i - h * hd; d[i] = s[h * 2u * hd + off + j]; }")))

    ; partial NEOX rope, in place: pair (k, k+nrot/2) inside the first nrot dims of each head,
    ; theta_k = pos * base^(-2k/nrot) over the body's fpow/fsin/fcos; dims past nrot untouched.
    (defn kth-prope-msl (fname)
        (str_concat "kernel void "
        (str_concat fname
            " (device float* v [[buffer(0)]], constant uint& nh [[buffer(1)]], constant uint& hd [[buffer(2)]], constant uint& nrot [[buffer(3)]], constant uint& pos [[buffer(4)]], constant float& base [[buffer(5)]], uint gid [[thread_position_in_grid]]) { uint np = nrot / 2u; if (gid >= nh * np) return; uint h = gid / np; uint k = gid - h * np; uint o = h * hd; float ex = (-2.0f * float(k)) / float(nrot); float fq = fpow(base, ex); float a = float(pos) * fq; float ca = fcos(a); float sa = fsin(a); uint i0 = o + k; uint i1 = o + k + np; float x0 = v[i0]; float x1 = v[i1]; float t0 = x0 * ca; float t1 = x1 * sa; v[i0] = t0 - t1; float t2 = x0 * sa; float t3 = x1 * ca; v[i1] = t2 + t3; }")))

    ; the full-attention output gate: x *= sigmoid(g). SIGMOID here (qwen35moe.cpp), silu on the
    ; deltanet side — the two must not be swapped and the band refuses the swap.
    (defn kth-sigmul-msl (fname)
        (str_concat "kernel void "
        (str_concat fname
            " (device float* x [[buffer(0)]], device const float* g [[buffer(1)]], constant uint& n [[buffer(2)]], uint i [[thread_position_in_grid]]) { if (i >= n) return; float zz = g[i]; float sg = 1.0f / (1.0f + fexp(-1.0f * zz)); x[i] = x[i] * sg; }")))

    ; the expert accumulation, weights READ FROM THE DEVICE (they were computed there; only the
    ; ids crossed): y = w[widx]*x sets, y += w[widx]*x accumulates — moe-msl's scale/axpy with
    ; the constant traded for a device word.
    (defn kth-scalew-msl (fname)
        (str_concat "kernel void "
        (str_concat fname
            " (device const float* x [[buffer(0)]], device float* y [[buffer(1)]], device const float* w [[buffer(2)]], constant uint& widx [[buffer(3)]], constant uint& n [[buffer(4)]], uint i [[thread_position_in_grid]]) { if (i >= n) return; y[i] = w[widx] * x[i]; }")))
    (defn kth-axpyw-msl (fname)
        (str_concat "kernel void "
        (str_concat fname
            " (device const float* x [[buffer(0)]], device float* y [[buffer(1)]], device const float* w [[buffer(2)]], constant uint& widx [[buffer(3)]], constant uint& n [[buffer(4)]], uint i [[thread_position_in_grid]]) { if (i >= n) return; float p = w[widx] * x[i]; y[i] = y[i] + p; }")))

    ; the shared expert's gate: y += sigmoid(s[0]) * x — one scalar dot, sigmoided, gating the
    ; whole shared path (qwen35moe.cpp's shared_expert_gate).
    (defn kth-axpysig-msl (fname)
        (str_concat "kernel void "
        (str_concat fname
            " (device const float* x [[buffer(0)]], device float* y [[buffer(1)]], device const float* s [[buffer(2)]], constant uint& n [[buffer(3)]], uint i [[thread_position_in_grid]]) { if (i >= n) return; float sg = 1.0f / (1.0f + fexp(-1.0f * s[0])); float p = sg * x[i]; y[i] = y[i] + p; }")))

    ; the cache placement move — llama-token-handle's kernel, authored here for the same
    ; fixed-offset-binding reason. No arithmetic.
    (defn kth-copyoff-msl (fname)
        (str_concat "kernel void "
        (str_concat fname
            " (device const float* s [[buffer(0)]], device float* d [[buffer(1)]], constant uint& n [[buffer(2)]], constant uint& doff [[buffer(3)]], uint i [[thread_position_in_grid]]) { if (i >= n) return; d[doff + i] = s[i]; }")))

    ; ================= the translation unit =================
    ; q80's spine carries the one q6k_mod/q6k_s8/q6k_f16/q6k_pow2 definition; q6m contributes its
    ; weight decode and matvec WITHOUT re-emitting that spine; ldm-msl-unit brings the
    ; transcendental spine (fexp/fln/fsin/fcos/fpow, round) once, plus rmsnorm (+tg twin), the
    ; GQA attention, swiglu, add, argmax (+two-stage twins). fp contraction off by pragma —
    ; kat-block0-handle's own rule, kept.
    (defn kth-msl ()
        (str_concat "#include <metal_stdlib>\n#pragma clang fp contract(off)\n"
        (str_concat (q80-msl-unit "form_q8_0_dequant_f32" "form_q8_0_matvec_f32" "form_q8_0_matvec_lane_f32")
        (str_concat "static inline float fh16(uint b) { return q6k_f16(int(b)); }"
        (str_concat (q3m-msl-appendix)
        (str_concat (q4m-msl-helpers)
        (str_concat (q4m-matvec-body "form_q4k_matvec_f32")
        (str_concat (q6m-msl-weight)
        (str_concat (q6m-matvec-body "form_q6k_matvec_f32")
        (str_concat (ldm-msl-unit)
        (str_concat (mla-matvec-body)
        ; the gdn cells' declared spine is fexp + fsqrt; fexp is ldm's, and fsqrt is emitted
        ; HERE as the body's own tn-sqrt transcription (Newton-50 from the value — the same
        ; fold mla_sqrt and dm_sqrt carry), NOT metal::sqrt: the attestant lane's shell spine
        ; reached for the vendor library and this unit keeps the determinism discipline instead.
        (str_concat "static inline float fsqrt(float v) { if (v <= 0.0f) return 0.0f; float g = v; for (int n = 0; n < 50; ++n) { g = 0.5f * (g + v / g); } return g; } "
        (str_concat (gdm-conv-msl   "form_gdn_conv_f32")
        (str_concat (gdm-l2norm-msl "form_gdn_l2norm_f32")
        (str_concat (mrw-msl-appendix)
        (str_concat (kth-q3krow-msl   "form_q3k_row_f32")
        (str_concat (kth-q4moff-msl   "form_q4k_matvec_off_f32")
        (str_concat (kth-q3moff-msl   "form_q3k_matvec_off_f32")
        (str_concat (kth-silu-msl     "form_silu_f32")
        (str_concat (kth-gates-msl    "form_gdn_gates_f32")
        (str_concat (kth-delta-msl    "form_gdn_delta_heads_f32")
        (str_concat (kth-gnorm-msl    "form_gdn_norm_gate_f32")
        (str_concat (kth-headrmsw-msl "form_headrms_w_f32")
        (str_concat (kth-qsplit-msl   "form_qsplit_f32")
        (str_concat (kth-prope-msl    "form_partial_rope_f32")
        (str_concat (kth-sigmul-msl   "form_sig_mul_f32")
        (str_concat (kth-scalew-msl   "form_scale_w_f32")
        (str_concat (kth-axpyw-msl    "form_axpy_w_f32")
        (str_concat (kth-axpysig-msl  "form_axpy_sig_f32")
                    (kth-copyoff-msl  "form_copy_off_f32"))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))

    ; ================= byte pricing, per declared ggml type =================
    ; 0 for anything unpriced, so an unknown type refuses to map (kat-exit-handle's rule).
    (defn kth-tybytes (ty n)
        (if (eq ty 0)  (mul n 4)
        (if (eq ty 8)  (mul (div n 32) 34)
        (if (eq ty 11) (mul (div n 256) 110)
        (if (eq ty 12) (mul (div n 256) 144)
        (if (eq ty 14) (mul (div n 256) 210)
            0))))))
    (defn kth-nw (src off)
        (do (let nd (egg-ti-ndims src off))
            (mul (egg-ti-dim src off 0)
            (mul (if (gt nd 1) (egg-ti-dim src off 1) 1)
                 (if (gt nd 2) (egg-ti-dim src off 2) 1)))))
    (defn kth-bytes (src off) (kth-tybytes (egg-ti-type src off) (kth-nw src off)))

    ; a tensor VIEW from a collected record offset: (handle rows cols type). rows is dim1 —
    ; for the 3D expert tensors that is the PER-EXPERT row count, and the expert lives in ebase.
    (defn kth-tv-at (src base path off)
        (list (metal_buf_from_file path (add base (egg-ti-dataoff src off)) (kth-bytes src off))
              (if (gt (egg-ti-ndims src off) 1) (egg-ti-dim src off 1) 1)
              (egg-ti-dim src off 0)
              (egg-ti-type src off)))
    (defn kth-tv-h  (t) (nth t 0))
    (defn kth-tv-r  (t) (nth t 1))
    (defn kth-tv-c  (t) (nth t 2))
    (defn kth-tv-ty (t) (nth t 3))

    ; ================= the layer schedule and the collected walks =================
    ; full attention every 4th block (the KV's own interval): (l+1) mod 4 == 0.
    (defn kth-full? (l interval) (eq (mod (add l 1) interval) 0))

    (defn kth-suffixes ()
        (list ".attn_norm.weight" ".post_attention_norm.weight"
              ".ffn_gate_inp.weight" ".ffn_gate_exps.weight" ".ffn_up_exps.weight"
              ".ffn_down_exps.weight" ".ffn_gate_inp_shexp.weight" ".ffn_gate_shexp.weight"
              ".ffn_up_shexp.weight" ".ffn_down_shexp.weight"
              ".attn_qkv.weight" ".ssm_conv1d.weight" ".ssm_alpha.weight" ".ssm_beta.weight"
              ".ssm_a" ".ssm_dt.bias" ".ssm_norm.weight" ".attn_gate.weight" ".ssm_out.weight"
              ".attn_q.weight" ".attn_k.weight" ".attn_v.weight" ".attn_q_norm.weight"
              ".attn_k_norm.weight" ".attn_output.weight"))
    (defn kth-tabs-go (src sfx acc)
        (if (eq (len sfx) 0) (reverse acc)
            (kth-tabs-go src (tail sfx) (cons (gti-offs-with src (head sfx)) acc))))
    (defn kth-tabs (src) (kth-tabs-go src (kth-suffixes) (empty)))

    (defn kth-tv-for (src base path tabs k l)
        (kth-tv-at src base path (gti-off-for (nth tabs k) l)))

    ; one layer's views. Common head: 0 attn_norm 1 post_norm, then the MoE nine
    ; (2 gate_inp 3 gexps 4 uexps 5 dexps 6 inp_shexp 7 gsh 8 ush 9 dsh), then the kind-specific
    ; tail: LINEAR 10 qkv 11 conv 12 alpha 13 beta 14 ssm_a 15 dtb 16 ssm_norm 17 z-gate 18 out;
    ; FULL 10 q 11 k 12 v 13 qnorm 14 knorm 15 wo.
    (defn kth-layer-common (src base path tabs l)
        (list (kth-tv-for src base path tabs 0 l)
              (kth-tv-for src base path tabs 1 l)
              (kth-tv-for src base path tabs 2 l)
              (kth-tv-for src base path tabs 3 l)
              (kth-tv-for src base path tabs 4 l)
              (kth-tv-for src base path tabs 5 l)
              (kth-tv-for src base path tabs 6 l)
              (kth-tv-for src base path tabs 7 l)
              (kth-tv-for src base path tabs 8 l)
              (kth-tv-for src base path tabs 9 l)))
    (defn kth-layer (src base path tabs l interval)
        (if (kth-full? l interval)
            (append (kth-layer-common src base path tabs l)
                    (list (kth-tv-for src base path tabs 19 l)
                          (kth-tv-for src base path tabs 20 l)
                          (kth-tv-for src base path tabs 21 l)
                          (kth-tv-for src base path tabs 22 l)
                          (kth-tv-for src base path tabs 23 l)
                          (kth-tv-for src base path tabs 24 l)))
            (append (kth-layer-common src base path tabs l)
                    (list (kth-tv-for src base path tabs 10 l)
                          (kth-tv-for src base path tabs 11 l)
                          (kth-tv-for src base path tabs 12 l)
                          (kth-tv-for src base path tabs 13 l)
                          (kth-tv-for src base path tabs 14 l)
                          (kth-tv-for src base path tabs 15 l)
                          (kth-tv-for src base path tabs 16 l)
                          (kth-tv-for src base path tabs 17 l)
                          (kth-tv-for src base path tabs 18 l)))))
    (defn kth-layers-go (src base path tabs l n interval acc)
        (if (ge l n) acc
            (kth-layers-go src base path tabs (add l 1) n interval
                (append acc (list (kth-layer src base path tabs l interval))))))
    (defn kth-layers (src base path n interval)
        (kth-layers-go src base path (kth-tabs src) 0 n interval (empty)))

    ; ================= the pool =================
    ; pipes: 0 q3row 1 q4mv 2 q4mvoff 3 q6mv 4 q80mv 5 rms 6 rmstg 7 conv 8 silu 9 l2 10 gates
    ;        11 delta 12 gnorm 13 headrmsw 14 qsplit 15 prope 16 gqa 17 sigmul 18 swiglu 19 add
    ;        20 route 21 scalew 22 axpyw 23 axpysig 24 copyoff 25 argpart 26 argcomb 27 f32mv 28 q3mvoff
    (defn kth-pipes (msl)
        (list (metal_pipeline msl "form_q3k_row_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_q4k_matvec_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_q4k_matvec_off_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_q6k_matvec_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_q8_0_matvec_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_rmsnorm_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_rmsnorm_tg_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_gdn_conv_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_silu_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_gdn_l2norm_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_gdn_gates_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_gdn_delta_heads_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_gdn_norm_gate_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_headrms_w_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_qsplit_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_partial_rope_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_gqa_decode_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_sig_mul_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_swiglu_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_add_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_moe_route_wide_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_scale_w_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_axpy_w_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_axpy_sig_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_copy_off_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_argmax_part_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_argmax_comb_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_mla_matvec_f32")
              (metal_pipeline msl "form_q3k_matvec_off_f32")))
    (defn kth-pipes-ok? (ps) (if (eq (len ps) 0) true (if (le (head ps) 0) false (kth-pipes-ok? (tail ps)))))

    ; bufs: 0 X 1 H 2 QKV(convdim) 3 A(nv) 4 B(nv) 5 Alpha 6 Beta 7 Z(dinner) 8 O(dinner)
    ;       9 G(dinner) 10 T(d) 11 Log(nExp) 12 Ids 13 Wts 14 Ge(ff) 15 Ue(ff) 16 Act(ff)
    ;       17 Eo(d) 18 MoE(d) 19 ShAct(ff) 20 ShOut(d) 21 ShGate 22 Q(nq*hd) 23 Gate(nq*hd)
    ;       24 K(kvd) 25 V(kvd) 26 Attn(nq*hd) 27 Scratch 28 Voc 29 Pi 30 Pv 31 OutI 32 OutV
    ; ── span-wide scratch ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
    ; Every buffer below that holds ONE position's working values is multiplied
    ; by `span`, token-major: slot i of token t lives at [t * n + i]. That is the
    ; layout the batched matmul already writes (y[t * rows + r]) and reads
    ; (x[t * cols + j]), so widening here is what lets a batched kernel be
    ; dispatched at all.
    ;
    ; Not widened: the two 32-byte and three 16-byte constant slots, the 4096
    ; scratch pair, the attention scratch at 27 (already 2*nq*maxpos, position
    ; wide by construction), and the vocab logits at 28 — prefill asks the head
    ; at one position only, so a span of logits would be allocated and unread.
    ;
    ; span 1 allocates exactly what kth-bufs always allocated.
    (defn kth-bufs-span (d convdim dinner nv ff nExp nqhd kvd maxpos nq vocabN span)
        (list (metal_buf_alloc (mul (mul d span) 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul (mul d span) 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul (mul convdim span) 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul (mul nv span) 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul (mul nv span) 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul (mul nv span) 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul (mul nv span) 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul (mul dinner span) 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul (mul dinner span) 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul (mul dinner span) 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul (mul d span) 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul (mul nExp span) 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc 32)
              (metal_buf_alloc 32)
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul (mul ff span) 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul (mul ff span) 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul (mul ff span) 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul (mul d span) 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul (mul d span) 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul (mul ff span) 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul (mul d span) 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc 16)
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul (mul nqhd span) 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul (mul nqhd span) 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul (mul kvd span) 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul (mul kvd span) 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul (mul nqhd span) 4))
              ; 27 — attention score scratch. Span-wide too: the span attention
              ; kernel gives every (token, head) its own row, so this is
              ; 2 * ntok * nq * maxpos rather than 2 * nq * maxpos.
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul (mul (mul (mul 2 nq) maxpos) span) 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul vocabN 4))
              (metal_buf_alloc 4096)
              (metal_buf_alloc 4096)
              (metal_buf_alloc 16)
              (metal_buf_alloc 16)
              ; 33 — the token-major residual stream for a layer-major walk.
              ; Attention runs one position at a time into slot 0's single-token
              ; working set; this is where each position's residual lives between
              ; layers, so a batched FFN can read the whole span at once.
              (metal_buf_alloc (mul (mul d span) 4))))

    (defn kth-bufs (d convdim dinner nv ff nExp nqhd kvd maxpos nq vocabN)
        (kth-bufs-span d convdim dinner nv ff nExp nqhd kvd maxpos nq vocabN 1))

    ; per-STREAM state: one conv window + one delta state per linear block, one K + one V cache
    ; per full block; indexed BY LAYER (non-owners carry 0, never dispatched). Zero-filled by
    ; the allocator, so a new stream needs no zeroing pass.
    (defn kth-state-go (l n interval convdim taps nv dv dk kvd maxpos acc)
        (if (ge l n) acc
            (kth-state-go (add l 1) n interval convdim taps nv dv dk kvd maxpos
                (append acc
                    (if (kth-full? l interval)
                        (list (list 0 0
                                    (metal_buf_alloc (mul (mul kvd maxpos) 4))
                                    (metal_buf_alloc (mul (mul kvd maxpos) 4))))
                        (list (list (metal_buf_alloc (mul (mul convdim taps) 4))
                                    (metal_buf_alloc (mul (mul (mul nv dv) dk) 4))
                                    0 0)))))))
    (defn kth-stream-state (n interval convdim taps nv dv dk kvd maxpos)
        (kth-state-go 0 n interval convdim taps nv dv dk kvd maxpos (empty)))

    ; ================= dispatch helpers =================
    ; SERIAL encoder, tpg 256 everywhere mode 0 runs (the proven 2.9x), barrier 0 (a serial
    ; batch refuses barriers, correctly — order is already total).
    (defn kth-b16 (bufs consts) (md-bind16 bufs consts 256 0 0 0))

    (defn kth-mv (ps tv xh yh)
        (metal_enqueue
            (if (eq (kth-tv-ty tv) 12) (nth ps 1)
            (if (eq (kth-tv-ty tv) 14) (nth ps 3)
            (if (eq (kth-tv-ty tv) 8)  (nth ps 4)
                                       (nth ps 27))))
            (kth-b16 (list (kth-tv-h tv) xh yh) (list (kth-tv-r tv) (kth-tv-c tv)))
            (kth-tv-r tv)))
    ; the expert matvec dispatches BY THE TENSOR'S OWN DECLARED TYPE — the census taught that
    ; the routed experts are Q3_K in thirty blocks and Q4_K in ten, so the type is per tensor,
    ; never per family.
    (defn kth-mvoff (ps tv xh yh ebase)
        (metal_enqueue (if (eq (kth-tv-ty tv) 11) (nth ps 28) (nth ps 2))
            (kth-b16 (list (kth-tv-h tv) xh yh) (list (kth-tv-r tv) (kth-tv-c tv) ebase))
            (kth-tv-r tv)))
    ; the cooperative RMSNorm twin: ONE threadgroup of 256 exactly, mode 1
    (defn kth-rms (ps xh gtv yh n epsBits)
        (metal_enqueue (nth ps 6)
            (md-bind16 (list xh (kth-tv-h gtv) yh) (list n epsBits) 256 0 1 0)
            1))
    (defn kth-el1 (ps p xh n) (metal_enqueue p (kth-b16 (list xh) (list n)) n))

    ; ================= one LINEAR block =================
    ; lay: see kth-layer. st: (win S 0 0).
    (defn kth-linear-attn (ps bs geo lay st)
        (do
            (kth-rms ps (nth bs 0) (nth lay 0) (nth bs 1) (nth geo 0) (nth geo 6))
            (kth-mv ps (nth lay 10) (nth bs 1) (nth bs 2))
            (kth-mv ps (nth lay 12) (nth bs 1) (nth bs 3))
            (kth-mv ps (nth lay 13) (nth bs 1) (nth bs 4))
            (kth-mv ps (nth lay 17) (nth bs 1) (nth bs 7))
            (metal_enqueue (nth ps 7)
                (kth-b16 (list (nth st 0) (nth bs 2) (kth-tv-h (nth lay 11)) (nth bs 2))
                         (list (nth geo 1) (nth geo 23)))
                (nth geo 1))
            (kth-el1 ps (nth ps 8) (nth bs 2) (nth geo 1))
            (metal_enqueue (nth ps 9)
                (kth-b16 (list (nth bs 2)) (list (mul 2 (nth geo 2)) (nth geo 4) (nth geo 6)))
                (mul 2 (nth geo 2)))
            (metal_enqueue (nth ps 10)
                (kth-b16 (list (nth bs 3) (nth bs 4) (kth-tv-h (nth lay 14)) (kth-tv-h (nth lay 15))
                               (nth bs 5) (nth bs 6))
                         (list (nth geo 3)))
                (nth geo 3))
            (metal_enqueue (nth ps 11)
                (kth-b16 (list (nth st 1) (nth bs 2) (nth bs 5) (nth bs 6) (nth bs 8))
                         (list (nth geo 3) (nth geo 5) (nth geo 4) (nth geo 2) (nth geo 7)))
                (mul (nth geo 3) (nth geo 5)))
            (metal_enqueue (nth ps 12)
                (kth-b16 (list (nth bs 8) (kth-tv-h (nth lay 16)) (nth bs 7) (nth bs 9))
                         (list (nth geo 3) (nth geo 5) (nth geo 6)))
                (nth geo 3))
            (kth-mv ps (nth lay 18) (nth bs 9) (nth bs 10))
            (metal_enqueue (nth ps 19)
                (kth-b16 (list (nth bs 0) (nth bs 10) (nth bs 0)) (list (nth geo 0)))
                (nth geo 0))
            1))

    ; NOTE ON THE CONV BINDING: the conv kernel reads x[c] and writes y[c] — it is dispatched
    ; with bQKV as BOTH: each thread reads its own x[c] BEFORE writing y[c], and thread c
    ; touches only channel c, so in-place is exact and saves a buffer the size of the
    ; concatenation. The window shift reads only win.

    ; ================= one FULL block =================
    ; st: (0 0 ck cv). geo indices: see the pool section.
    (defn kth-full-attn (ps bs geo lay st pos)
        (do
            (kth-rms ps (nth bs 0) (nth lay 0) (nth bs 1) (nth geo 0) (nth geo 6))
            (kth-mv ps (nth lay 10) (nth bs 1) (nth bs 2))
            (kth-mv ps (nth lay 11) (nth bs 1) (nth bs 24))
            (kth-mv ps (nth lay 12) (nth bs 1) (nth bs 25))
            (metal_enqueue (nth ps 14)
                (kth-b16 (list (nth bs 2) (nth bs 22))
                         (list (mul (nth geo 12) (nth geo 14)) (nth geo 14) 0))
                (mul (nth geo 12) (nth geo 14)))
            (metal_enqueue (nth ps 14)
                (kth-b16 (list (nth bs 2) (nth bs 23))
                         (list (mul (nth geo 12) (nth geo 14)) (nth geo 14) (nth geo 14)))
                (mul (nth geo 12) (nth geo 14)))
            (metal_enqueue (nth ps 13)
                (kth-b16 (list (nth bs 22) (kth-tv-h (nth lay 13)) (nth bs 22))
                         (list (nth geo 12) (nth geo 14) (nth geo 6)))
                (nth geo 12))
            (metal_enqueue (nth ps 13)
                (kth-b16 (list (nth bs 24) (kth-tv-h (nth lay 14)) (nth bs 24))
                         (list (nth geo 13) (nth geo 14) (nth geo 6)))
                (nth geo 13))
            (metal_enqueue (nth ps 15)
                (kth-b16 (list (nth bs 22))
                         (list (nth geo 12) (nth geo 14) (nth geo 15) pos (nth geo 16)))
                (mul (nth geo 12) (div (nth geo 15) 2)))
            (metal_enqueue (nth ps 15)
                (kth-b16 (list (nth bs 24))
                         (list (nth geo 13) (nth geo 14) (nth geo 15) pos (nth geo 16)))
                (mul (nth geo 13) (div (nth geo 15) 2)))
            (metal_enqueue (nth ps 24)
                (kth-b16 (list (nth bs 24) (nth st 2)) (list (nth geo 20) (mul pos (nth geo 20))))
                (nth geo 20))
            (metal_enqueue (nth ps 24)
                (kth-b16 (list (nth bs 25) (nth st 3)) (list (nth geo 20) (mul pos (nth geo 20))))
                (nth geo 20))
            (metal_enqueue (nth ps 16)
                (kth-b16 (list (nth bs 22) (nth st 2) (nth st 3) (nth bs 26) (nth bs 27))
                         (list (add pos 1) (nth geo 12) (nth geo 13) (nth geo 14)
                               (nth geo 17) (nth geo 18)))
                (nth geo 12))
            (metal_enqueue (nth ps 17)
                (kth-b16 (list (nth bs 26) (nth bs 23)) (list (mul (nth geo 12) (nth geo 14))))
                (mul (nth geo 12) (nth geo 14)))
            (kth-mv ps (nth lay 15) (nth bs 26) (nth bs 10))
            (metal_enqueue (nth ps 19)
                (kth-b16 (list (nth bs 0) (nth bs 10) (nth bs 0)) (list (nth geo 0)))
                (nth geo 0))
            1))

    ; ================= the MoE half, shared by every block =================
    ; the routing ids are the ONE mid-block readback: 32 bytes, so the host can bind eight
    ; expert offsets. The weights never cross — scale_w/axpy_w read them where they were born.
    (defn kth-u32at (s i)
        (add (str_byte_at s (mul i 4))
        (add (mul (str_byte_at s (add (mul i 4) 1)) 256)
        (add (mul (str_byte_at s (add (mul i 4) 2)) 65536)
             (mul (str_byte_at s (add (mul i 4) 3)) 16777216)))))

    (defn kth-experts-go (ps bs geo lay ids k)
        (if (ge k (nth geo 9)) 1
            (do (let e (kth-u32at ids k))
                (let ebase (mul e (mul (nth geo 10) (nth geo 0))))
                (kth-mvoff ps (nth lay 3) (nth bs 1) (nth bs 14) ebase)
                (kth-mvoff ps (nth lay 4) (nth bs 1) (nth bs 15) ebase)
                (metal_enqueue (nth ps 18)
                    (kth-b16 (list (nth bs 14) (nth bs 15) (nth bs 16)) (list (nth geo 10)))
                    (nth geo 10))
                (kth-mvoff ps (nth lay 5) (nth bs 16) (nth bs 17) ebase)
                (metal_enqueue (if (eq k 0) (nth ps 21) (nth ps 22))
                    (kth-b16 (list (nth bs 17) (nth bs 18) (nth bs 13)) (list k (nth geo 0)))
                    (nth geo 0))
                (kth-experts-go ps bs geo lay ids (add k 1)))))

    (defn kth-moe (ps bs geo lay)
        (do
            (kth-rms ps (nth bs 0) (nth lay 1) (nth bs 1) (nth geo 0) (nth geo 6))
            (kth-mv ps (nth lay 2) (nth bs 1) (nth bs 11))
            (metal_enqueue (nth ps 20)
                (kth-b16 (list (nth bs 11) (nth bs 12) (nth bs 13))
                         (list (nth geo 8) (nth geo 9)))
                1)
            ; THE BLOCK'S ONE SYNC: eight ids cross, nothing else
            (let ids (metal_buf_read (nth bs 12) 0 32))
            (kth-experts-go ps bs geo lay ids 0)
            ; the shared expert, gated by its own sigmoided scalar
            (kth-mv ps (nth lay 7) (nth bs 1) (nth bs 14))
            (kth-mv ps (nth lay 8) (nth bs 1) (nth bs 15))
            (metal_enqueue (nth ps 18)
                (kth-b16 (list (nth bs 14) (nth bs 15) (nth bs 19)) (list (nth geo 11)))
                (nth geo 11))
            (kth-mv ps (nth lay 9) (nth bs 19) (nth bs 20))
            (kth-mv ps (nth lay 6) (nth bs 1) (nth bs 21))
            (metal_enqueue (nth ps 23)
                (kth-b16 (list (nth bs 20) (nth bs 18) (nth bs 21)) (list (nth geo 0)))
                (nth geo 0))
            (metal_enqueue (nth ps 19)
                (kth-b16 (list (nth bs 0) (nth bs 18) (nth bs 0)) (list (nth geo 0)))
                (nth geo 0))
            1))

    ; ================= one token =================
    (defn kth-blocks (ps bs geo lays sts pos l n interval)
        (if (ge l n) 1
            (do (if (kth-full? l interval)
                    (kth-full-attn ps bs geo (nth lays l) (nth sts l) pos)
                    (kth-linear-attn ps bs geo (nth lays l) (nth sts l)))
                (kth-moe ps bs geo (nth lays l))
                (kth-blocks ps bs geo lays sts pos (add l 1) n interval))))

    (defn kth-head (ps bs geo onormTv projTv)
        (do
            (kth-rms ps (nth bs 0) onormTv (nth bs 1) (nth geo 0) (nth geo 6))
            (kth-mv ps projTv (nth bs 1) (nth bs 28))
            (metal_enqueue (nth ps 25)
                (kth-b16 (list (nth bs 28) (nth bs 29) (nth bs 30)) (list (nth geo 19) 1024))
                1024)
            (metal_enqueue (nth ps 26)
                (md-bind16 (list (nth bs 29) (nth bs 30) (nth bs 31) (nth bs 32))
                           (list 1024) 1024 0 1 0)
                1)
            0))

    ; embed -> 40 blocks -> exit head -> FOUR BYTES. embTv is the whole resident Q3_K table;
    ; the token is a superblock offset into it, never a new view.
    (defn kth-forward (ps bs geo lays sts embTv onormTv projTv id pos)
        (do
            (metal_enqueue (nth ps 0)
                (kth-b16 (list (kth-tv-h embTv) (nth bs 0))
                         (list (mul id (div (nth geo 0) 256)) (nth geo 0)))
                (nth geo 0))
            (kth-blocks ps bs geo lays sts pos 0 (nth geo 21) (nth geo 22))
            (kth-head ps bs geo onormTv projTv)
            (kth-u32at (metal_buf_read (nth bs 31) 0 4) 0)))

    ; ================= the loop, in the body =================
    (defn kth-generate (ps bs geo lays sts embTv onormTv projTv id pos n acc)
        (if (le n 0) acc
            (do (let nid (kth-forward ps bs geo lays sts embTv onormTv projTv id pos))
                (if (lt nid 0) acc
                    (kth-generate ps bs geo lays sts embTv onormTv projTv
                                  nid (add pos 1) (sub n 1) (append acc (list nid)))))))

    (defn kth-prefill (ps bs geo lays sts embTv onormTv projTv ids pos)
        (if (eq (len ids) 1)
            (list (kth-forward ps bs geo lays sts embTv onormTv projTv (head ids) pos) (add pos 1))
            (do (kth-forward ps bs geo lays sts embTv onormTv projTv (head ids) pos)
                (kth-prefill ps bs geo lays sts embTv onormTv projTv (tail ids) (add pos 1)))))

    ; ================= the one setup, shared by band and run cells =================
    ; Every number below is the file's: the KVs name the geometry, the tensor table names every
    ; offset, dimension and type. Returns (ps bs geo lays embTv onormTv projTv src base).
    ; geo: 0 d 1 convdim 2 nkh 3 nvh 4 dk 5 dv 6 epsBits 7 qscaleBits 8 nExp 9 nSel 10 expFF
    ;      11 shFF 12 nHead 13 nKV 14 headDim 15 nrot 16 ropeBaseBits 17 attnScaleBits
    ;      18 maxpos 19 vocabN 20 kvd 21 nLayer 22 interval 23 taps
    (defn kth-geo (src maxpos)
        (do
            (let d (gmt-u32 src "qwen35moe.embedding_length"))
            (let nkh (gmt-u32 src "qwen35moe.ssm.group_count"))
            (let nvh (gmt-u32 src "qwen35moe.ssm.time_step_rank"))
            (let dk (gmt-u32 src "qwen35moe.ssm.state_size"))
            (let dinner (gmt-u32 src "qwen35moe.ssm.inner_size"))
            (let dv (div dinner nvh))
            (let taps (gmt-u32 src "qwen35moe.ssm.conv_kernel"))
            (let eps (gmt-f32 src "qwen35moe.attention.layer_norm_rms_epsilon"))
            (let nHead (gmt-u32 src "qwen35moe.attention.head_count"))
            (let nKV (gmt-u32 src "qwen35moe.attention.head_count_kv"))
            (let headDim (gmt-u32 src "qwen35moe.attention.key_length"))
            (let nrot (gmt-u32 src "qwen35moe.rope.dimension_count"))
            (let base (gmt-f32 src "qwen35moe.rope.freq_base"))
            (let nLayerAll (gmt-u32 src "qwen35moe.block_count"))
            (let nextn (gmt-u32 src "qwen35moe.nextn_predict_layers"))
            (list d
                  (add (mul 2 (mul nkh dk)) dinner)
                  nkh nvh dk dv
                  (md-f32-bits eps)
                  (md-f32-bits (div 1.0 (math_sqrt (add dk 0.0))))
                  (gmt-u32 src "qwen35moe.expert_count")
                  (gmt-u32 src "qwen35moe.expert_used_count")
                  (gmt-u32 src "qwen35moe.expert_feed_forward_length")
                  (gmt-u32 src "qwen35moe.expert_shared_feed_forward_length")
                  nHead nKV headDim nrot
                  (md-f32-bits base)
                  (md-f32-bits (div 1.0 (math_sqrt (add headDim 0.0))))
                  maxpos
                  (gmt-vocab-n src)
                  (mul nKV headDim)
                  (sub nLayerAll nextn)
                  (gmt-u32 src "qwen35moe.full_attention_interval")
                  taps)))

    (defn kth-setup (maxpos)
        (do
            (let path (kce-path))
            (let src (kce-hdr))
            (let base (egg-data-base src (kce-align)))
            (let geo (kth-geo src maxpos))
            (let ps (kth-pipes (kth-msl)))
            (let bs (kth-bufs (nth geo 0) (nth geo 1) (mul (nth geo 3) (nth geo 5)) (nth geo 3)
                              (nth geo 10) (nth geo 8) (mul (nth geo 12) (nth geo 14))
                              (nth geo 20) maxpos (nth geo 12) (nth geo 19)))
            (let lays (kth-layers src base path (nth geo 21) (nth geo 22)))
            (let embTv (kth-tv-at src base path (egg-find-tensor src "token_embd.weight")))
            (let onormTv (kth-tv-at src base path (egg-find-tensor src "output_norm.weight")))
            (let projTv (kth-tv-at src base path (egg-find-tensor src "output.weight")))
            (list ps bs geo lays embTv onormTv projTv src base)))

    (defn kth-new-state (geo)
        (kth-stream-state (nth geo 21) (nth geo 22) (nth geo 1) (nth geo 23)
                          (nth geo 3) (nth geo 5) (nth geo 4) (nth geo 20) (nth geo 18)))
    0)
